   "text": "I read the drawing as a 13-residue cyclic peptide (a cyclosporin-like ring) and traced it clockwise from the N-methylalanine near the top. The sequence is:\n\nN-Me-Ala, N-Me-Phe, Ala, N-Me-Leu, Thr, Phe, N-Me-Ile, N-Me-Ala, N-Me-Leu, Ser(OtBu), N-Me-Leu, then Asp.\n\nThe Asp carries a piperidine amide on its \u03b1-carbonyl. Its side-chain carbonyl closes the ring onto the first N-Me-Ala nitrogen.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** I worked out each centre from the hashed and wedged bonds. All \u03b1-carbons come out as the natural L (S) configuration. The Thr \u03b2-carbon (OH wedge) is R and the Ile \u03b2-carbon (methyl hash) is S, consistent with L-Thr and L-Ile.\n\n**Uncertain centres:** The Ala \u03b1-carbon and the Phe \u03b1-carbon are the least clear in the drawing. I took both as L.\n\nThe Asp centre needed [C@H] rather than [C@@H] because I wrote its two carbon substituents in the opposite order from the usual L-Asp SMILES.\n\nSMILES: CN1[C@@H](C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](Cc2ccccc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccccc2)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H]([C@@H](C)CC)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](COC(C)(C)C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N[C@H](C(=O)N2CCCCC2)CC1=O"
